cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "SOZLab: GUI and CLI for solvent occupancy zone analysis of molecular dynamics trajectories"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Ferreira Francisco"
    given-names: "Aleff"
version: 2.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-20
url: "https://github.com/aleff-ferreira/SOZLab"
repository-code: "https://github.com/aleff-ferreira/SOZLab"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  SOZLab shows where the solvent is around part of a molecule in molecular dynamics trajectories and measures it:
  how many molecules are in a zone, how long they stay, how often they exchange, and where the solvent density is
  enriched. Every number is reported with its unit, an uncertainty and a note on when it can be trusted; every export
  records the software, settings and input files (SHA-256) that produced it. A Workbench GUI (live 3D zone, live
  occupancy preview, run comparison) and a CLI share one engine and give identical results.
keywords:
  - solvent
  - occupancy
  - residence time
  - molecular dynamics
  - MDAnalysis
  - GROMACS
  - hydration shell
  - reproducibility
